From a@stoney.io  Tue Sep  1 02:28:42 2015  Tue Sep  1 02:28:42 2015
From: a@stoney.io (Andrew Stone) (Andrew Stone)
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2015 20:28:42 -0400
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] rtmp: support the AMF_DATE tag
Message-ID: <1441067322-7457-1-git-send-email-a@stoney.io>

Instead of returning EINVAL, which can cause a stream to fail to load, this
allows the tag to be passed through to the flv demuxer, where it's summarily
ignored.
---
 libavformat/rtmppkt.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/libavformat/rtmppkt.c b/libavformat/rtmppkt.c
index c474fb3..0d693c2 100644
--- a/libavformat/rtmppkt.c
+++ b/libavformat/rtmppkt.c
@@ -440,6 +440,7 @@ int ff_amf_tag_size(const uint8_t *data, const uint8_t *data_end)
     case AMF_DATA_TYPE_STRING:      return 3 + AV_RB16(data);
     case AMF_DATA_TYPE_LONG_STRING: return 5 + AV_RB32(data);
     case AMF_DATA_TYPE_NULL:        return 1;
+    case AMF_DATA_TYPE_DATE:        return 11;
     case AMF_DATA_TYPE_ARRAY:
         parse_key = 0;
     case AMF_DATA_TYPE_MIXEDARRAY:
-- 
2.5.0


