From alex@sighthound.com  Sun Sep 13 02:25:12 2015  Sun Sep 13 02:25:12 2015
From: alex@sighthound.com (Alex Agranovsky) (Alex Agranovsky)
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2015 20:25:12 -0400
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] mpjpeg: CRLF terminating a sequence of
 MIME headers should not cause an error
In-Reply-To: <20150913001255.GQ4540@nb4>
References: <etPan.55f4902d.3d346790.fca3@alex-mbp13.agranovsky.com>
 <etPan.55f49380.1142be59.fca3@alex-mbp13.agranovsky.com>
 <20150912215357.GN4540@nb4>
 <etPan.55f4af7a.1b807c4b.fca3@alex-mbp13.agranovsky.com>
 <20150913001255.GQ4540@nb4>
Message-ID: <etPan.55f4c268.3c88d318.fca3@alex-mbp13.agranovsky.com>

This is as intended: stopping at the empty line is exactly what we should do in this case, as it separates headers from the content.
If the two headers we’re looking for hadn’t been encountered prior to the empty line, error should be returned. 

This is based on http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc2046:

    body-part := MIME-part-headers [CRLF *OCTET]
                  ; Lines in a body-part must not start
                  ; with the specified dash-boundary and
                  ; the delimiter must not appear anywhere
                  ; in the body part.  Note that the
                  ; semantics of a body-part differ from
                  ; the semantics of a message, as
                  ; described in the text.


-- 
Alex Agranovsky
Sighthound, Inc
www.sighthound.com		

