> > But now you can't spot unused functions anymore if you compile with
> > threading enabled, so what the hell is the point at all?
>
> I do not understand your comment: av_unused is a local thing; it
> applies only to the function under consideration. If I add an unused
> function static int foo, it will certainly spot it. Thus, unused
> functions can certainly be spotted; the only ones changed are the
> threading functions.


I had the same concern actually, so I'm actually glad I'm not the first to
say it :). The advantage of #if HAVE_THREADS around these threading
functions is that it allows us to spot these functions as being unused if
we ever make changes to the threading implementation. av_unused should be
used more like a second option. I prefer #if HAVE_THREADS in this
particular case...

Ronald

