From gajjanagadde@gmail.com  Thu Oct 15 03:54:17 2015  Thu Oct 15 03:54:17 2015
From: gajjanagadde@gmail.com (Ganesh Ajjanagadde) (Ganesh Ajjanagadde)
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2015 21:54:17 -0400
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] doc/ffmpeg: use stream_loop instead of loop
Message-ID: <1444874057-20248-1-git-send-email-gajjanagadde@gmail.com>

Commit dbb03b8e47f905f0f7b10c3eb5ac11f9bfc793ff renamed loop to
stream_loop. This documents the change.

Signed-off-by: Ganesh Ajjanagadde <gajjanagadde at gmail.com>
---
 doc/ffmpeg.texi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/ffmpeg.texi b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
index 5624930..de49618 100644
--- a/doc/ffmpeg.texi
+++ b/doc/ffmpeg.texi
@@ -253,7 +253,7 @@ Overwrite output files without asking.
 Do not overwrite output files, and exit immediately if a specified
 output file already exists.
 
- at item -loop @var{number} (@emph{input})
+ at item -stream_loop @var{number} (@emph{input})
 Set number of times input stream shall be looped.
 
 @item -c[:@var{stream_specifier}] @var{codec} (@emph{input/output,per-stream})
-- 
2.6.1


