I guess it´s a good idea to be more specify here, please see

https://software.intel.com/sites/default/files/mediasdk-man.pdf

page 129

Y, U, V, A;
R, G, B, A;
Y, Cr, Cb, A;
Y, CbCr;
Y, CrCb;
Y, UV;
Y, VU;
Data pointers to corresponding color channels. The frame buffer pointers
must be 16-byte aligned. The application has to specify pointers to all
color channels even for packed formats. For example, for YUY2 format
the application has to specify Y, U and V

This is also the case for RGB32, where PIX_FMT_RGB32 should be used as I did.
Will summarize this, update my patch and send it again ASAP.

