From jamrial@gmail.com  Sun Oct 25 00:08:37 2015  Sun Oct 25 00:08:37 2015
From: jamrial@gmail.com (James Almer) (James Almer)
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2015 19:08:37 -0300
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] x86/intmath: allow the source operand for
	icc/icl ff_ctzll to be a memory location
Message-ID: <1445724517-7148-1-git-send-email-jamrial@gmail.com>

This gives the compiler some flexibility

Signed-off-by: James Almer <jamrial at gmail.com>
---
 libavutil/x86/intmath.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/x86/intmath.h b/libavutil/x86/intmath.h
index 7881e3c..10d3e7f 100644
--- a/libavutil/x86/intmath.h
+++ b/libavutil/x86/intmath.h
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ static av_always_inline av_const int ff_ctzll_x86(long long v)
 {
 #   if ARCH_X86_64
     uint64_t c;
-    __asm__("bsfq %1,%0" : "=r" (c) : "r" (v));
+    __asm__ ("bsfq %1,%0" : "=r" (c) : "rm" (v));
     return c;
 #   else
     return ((uint32_t)v == 0) ? _bit_scan_forward((uint32_t)(v >> 32)) + 32 : _bit_scan_forward((uint32_t)v);
-- 
2.6.2


