From andreas.cadhalpun@googlemail.com  Sun Nov  8 00:08:54 2015  Sun Nov  8 00:08:54 2015
From: andreas.cadhalpun@googlemail.com (Andreas Cadhalpun) (Andreas Cadhalpun)
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2015 00:08:54 +0100
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH 3/4] softfloat: fix av_add_sf if one argument
	is zero
In-Reply-To: <563E841C.6020409@googlemail.com>
References: <563E841C.6020409@googlemail.com>
Message-ID: <563E8486.6090309@googlemail.com>

Otherwise (0x20000000, 1) + (0, 33) gives (0, 33), i.e. 1 + 0 = 0.

This fixes a division by zero in the aac_fixed decoder.

Signed-off-by: Andreas Cadhalpun <Andreas.Cadhalpun at googlemail.com>
---
 libavutil/softfloat.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavutil/softfloat.h b/libavutil/softfloat.h
index e87cbf4..fefde8c 100644
--- a/libavutil/softfloat.h
+++ b/libavutil/softfloat.h
@@ -130,7 +130,9 @@ static inline av_const int av_gt_sf(SoftFloat a, SoftFloat b)
 
 static inline av_const SoftFloat av_add_sf(SoftFloat a, SoftFloat b){
     int t= a.exp - b.exp;
-    if      (t <-31) return b;
+    if      (a.mant == 0) return b;
+    else if (b.mant == 0) return a;
+    else if (t <-31) return b;
     else if (t <  0) return av_normalize_sf(av_normalize1_sf((SoftFloat){ b.mant + (a.mant >> (-t)), b.exp}));
     else if (t < 32) return av_normalize_sf(av_normalize1_sf((SoftFloat){ a.mant + (b.mant >>   t ), a.exp}));
     else             return a;
-- 
2.6.2



From andreas.cadhalpun@googlemail.com  Sun Nov  8 00:09:02 2015  Sun Nov  8 00:09:02 2015
From: andreas.cadhalpun@googlemail.com (Andreas Cadhalpun) (Andreas Cadhalpun)
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2015 00:09:02 +0100
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH 4/4] softfloat: return one when the argument
 of av_sqrt_sf is negative
