From michael@niedermayer.cc  Tue Nov 10 00:34:24 2015  Tue Nov 10 00:34:24 2015
From: michael@niedermayer.cc (Michael Niedermayer) (Michael Niedermayer)
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2015 00:34:24 +0100
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] avformat/mp3dec: prefer "fast_seek" to
	TOC seek for CBR files.
In-Reply-To: <1446686517-32619-1-git-send-email-chcunningham@chromium.org>
References: <1446686517-32619-1-git-send-email-chcunningham@chromium.org>
Message-ID: <20151109233424.GO4540@nb4>

On Wed, Nov 04, 2015 at 05:21:57PM -0800, Chris Cunningham wrote:
> "Fast seek" uses linear interpolation to find the position of the
> requested seek time. For CBR this is more direct than using the
> mp3 TOC and bypassing the TOC avoids problems when the TOC is
