From atomnuker@gmail.com  Sat Nov 28 00:14:43 2015  Sat Nov 28 00:14:43 2015
From: atomnuker@gmail.com (Rostislav Pehlivanov) (Rostislav Pehlivanov)
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2015 23:14:43 +0000
Subject: [FFmpeg-devel] [PATCH] avcodec/aac_tablegen: get rid of
 hardcoded tables entirely
In-Reply-To: <1448662054-9635-1-git-send-email-gajjanagadde@gmail.com>
References: <1448662054-9635-1-git-send-email-gajjanagadde@gmail.com>
Message-ID: <1448666083.28849.6.camel@gmail.com>

On Fri, 2015-11-27 at 17:07 -0500, Ganesh Ajjanagadde wrote:
> Commit 96786a12f6df26990bbe7c0ca4592b3731724469 makes runtime
> initialization cheap.

Leaves a lot of the cruft around. aac_tablegen.h and
aac_tablegen_decl.h are now quite unnecessary. I suggest getting rid of
aac_tablegen* entirely and just moving everything entirely to aactab.h.
Just move the function as a normal function in aactab.c (or just define
it as a static inline in aactab.h since it's used only twice), define
the 2 tables there and you'd be done.

From gajjanagadde@gmail.com  Sat Nov 28 01:35:20 2015  Sat Nov 28 01:35:20 2015
From: gajjanagadde@gmail.com (Ganesh Ajjanagadde) (Ganesh Ajjanagadde)
